            <ArticleTitle>[Subacute intracoronary stent thrombosis in a patient with polycythaemia vera].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4104-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Polycythaemia vera is a myeloproliferative syndrome with thromboembolic and haemorrhagic complications. We describe a patient with polycythaemia vera and acute coronary syndrome in whom two-vessel intracoronary stent thrombosis occurred a few hours after percutaneous coronary intervention. The case was successfully treated by repeated stenting and abciximab infusion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
